ghly an 80% chance.\n\nPerriello has out-raised McGuire and holds a large cash advantage, and he has campaigned with Governor Spanberger, but the district's lean and incumbency remain significant obstacles. The only available poll, sponsored by a Democratic firm in early August, showed a narrow three-point Republican lead. The race is rated Lean Republican with meaningful uncertainty given the thin polling.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1914, "margin": -5.2}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2771, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.2238, "margin": -5.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.2476, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.2003, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.1957, "margin": -5.0}]}